X F3800 3,840 Wh 6,000 W 9,000 W 132.3 lb 60 kg $2,199.99 $0.57 \n Anker SOLIX F3800 Plus 3,840 Wh 6,000 W 9,000 W 136.7 lb 62 kg $2,699.99 $0.70 \n BLUETTI Elite 400 3,840 Wh 2,600 W 5,200 W 86 lb 39 kg $1,399 $0.36 \n Goal Zero Yeti PRO 4000 3,994 Wh 3,600 W 7,200 W 115.7 lb 52.5 kg $3,999.95 $1.00 \n EcoFlow DELTA Pro 3 4,096 Wh 4,000 W 8,000 W 113.5 lb 51.5 kg $3,699 $0.90 \n OUPES Guardian 6000 V2 4,608 Wh 6,000 W 9,000 W 111.8 lb 50.7 kg $2,699 $0.59 \n Jackery Explorer 5000 Plus 5,040 Wh 7,200 W 14,400 W 134.5 lb 61 kg $3,499 $0.69 \n EcoFlow DELTA Pro Ultra sold as separate pieces 6,144 Wh 7,200 W 10,800 W 181.7 lb 82.4 kg $5,799 $0.94 \n EcoFlow DELTA Pro Ultra X sold as separate pieces 12,288 Wh 12,000 W not published 298.7 lb 135.5 kg $7,999 $0.65 \n Every one uses lithium iron phosphate (LiFePO4) cells, so chemistry does not split the list.\n 2 entries are home backup systems sold as separate pieces, an inverter and battery packs (EcoFlow DELTA Pro Ultra and EcoFlow DELTA Pro Ultra X); their weights are the total of the pieces.\n Prices come from each maker's US store with the month we saw them: the list price where the store shows one, else the price shown on the maker's page. Sale prices change often and are not stored.\n By size\n What a 300 Wh station runs 6 models under 400 Wh \n What a 500 Wh station runs 4 models from 400 to 749 Wh \n What a 1,000 Wh station runs 13 models from 750 to 1,499 Wh \n What a 2,000 Wh station runs 13 models from 1,500 to 2,499 Wh \n What a 3,000 Wh station runs 13 models from 2,500 to 3,999 Wh \n What a 5,000 Wh station runs 5 models of 4,000 Wh and more \n Prices per Wh by size class : the median and the lowest stored price for each size, and the price at which each model would match them.\n Side by side\n Two stations from different brands in the same size class, with the same appliances run on both. No overall winner, one line per criterion.\n BLUETTI Elite 30 V2 vs Jackery Explorer 300 v2 \n EcoFlow RIVER 3 Plus vs 